  "exercise": {
    "summary": "Implement serialize(root) -> str and deserialize(data) -> root for a binary tree whose nodes have .val (an int), .left and .right. deserialize may return any node objects with those attributes (e.g. types.SimpleNamespace). deserialize(serialize(t)) must rebuild t's structure and values exactly. Explain how null markers let a single preorder walk be decoded unambiguously.",
